          <li>Filter small blood clots from the bloodstream<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Help regulate blood pH<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd2c Main Parts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Trachea (Windpipe):<\\/strong> Carries air to the lungs<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Bronchi:<\\/strong> Two tubes that branch into each lung<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Bronchioles:<\\/strong> Smaller branches inside the lungs<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Alveoli:<\\/strong> Tiny air sacs where gas exchange happens<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Diaphragm:<\\/strong> Muscle that helps you breathe<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udca1 Amazing Facts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Your lungs contain ~600 million alveoli \\u2013 if spread out, they would cover a tennis court!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>You breathe about 22,000 times per day<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The left lung is smaller than the right to make room for your heart<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Lungs are the only organ that can float on water<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your lungs produce about 1-2 liters of mucus daily (you swallow it without noticing)<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related System<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/respiratory-system\\\" style=\\\"background: #44aaff; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\\\">\\ud83e\\udec1 Respiratory System<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1714,200,'footnotes',''),(1716,201,'footnotes',''),(1720,203,'footnotes',''),(1721,198,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(1722,198,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(1723,198,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(1724,198,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:997ef14e505ddd4af49c620835e30da6'),(1725,204