/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 Functions<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Brings oxygen into the body for energy production<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Removes carbon dioxide (waste product from metabolism)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Filters and humidifies incoming air<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Helps regulate blood pH balance<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Allows you to speak (air passes through vocal cords)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Protects against airborne germs and particles<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udca1 Amazing Facts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Your lungs contain about 600 million alveoli \\u2013 if spread out, they would cover a tennis court!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>You breathe about 22,000 times per day (over 8 million times per year)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The left lung is smaller than the right to make room for your heart<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Lungs are the only organ that can float on water<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>A person breathes about 2,100 gallons of air every day<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your lungs produce about 1-2 liters of mucus daily (you swallow it without noticing)<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Organs<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/lungs\\\" style=\\\"background: #44aaff; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83e\\udec1 Lungs<\\/a>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Systems<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/circulatory-system\\\" style=\\\"background: #44aaff; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\u2764\\ufe0f Circulatory System<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(2055,241,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2056,241,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2057,241,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2058,241,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:6235a6c47f65a3aca2fc5a7c56ad64e4'),(2059,241,'_wp_page_template','default'),(2060,241,'_elementor_page_settings','a:1:{s:10:\"hide_title\";s:3:\"yes\";}'),(2062,242,'_edit_lock','1781558137:1'),(2064,242,'_eb_attr',''),(2065,242,'footnotes',''),(2066,242,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(2067,242,'_elementor_template_type','wp-page'),(2068,242,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"0d9124b\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":{\"content_width\":\"full\",\"width\":{\"unit\":\"%\",\"size\":93.98},\"_flex_size\":\"none\",\"_element_width\":\"initial\"},\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"d070d25\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"html\":\"<div style=\\\"max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; background: #e8ffe8;\\\">\\r\\n    <h1 style=\\\"color: #44aa44;\\\">\\u26a1 Nervous System<\\/h1>\\r\\n    \\r\\n    <div style=\\\"background: #000; border-radius: 15px; margin: 20px 0; overflow: hidden;\\\">\\r\\n        <iframe src=\\\"https:\\/\\/sketchfab.com\\/models\\/2e6be1399756494b9f185ce8c5900911\\/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\\\"\\r\\n            style=\\\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\\\" \\r\\n            allow=\\\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\\\" \\r\\n            allowfullscreen>\\r\\n        <\\/iframe>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n\\r\\n    <div style=\\\"background: white; padding: 20px; border-radius: 15px;\\\">\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 What is the Nervous System?<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <p>The nervous system is the command center of your body. It controls your thoughts, movements, breathing, heartbeat, and senses. It sends and receives signals throughout your body instantly.<\\/p>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd2c Main Parts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Brain:<\\/strong> Control center \\u2013 processes information and sends commands<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Spinal Cord:<\\/strong> Information highway \\u2013 connects brain to the body<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Nerves:<\\/strong> Cables that carry signals to and from the brain<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Neurons (Nerve Cells):<\\/strong> Individual cells that transmit electrical signals<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Synapses:<\\/strong> Gaps between neurons where signals jump across<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 Functions<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Controls all voluntary movements (walking, talking, writing)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Regulates involuntary functions (heartbeat, breathing, digestion)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Processes sensory information (sight, sound, touch, taste, smell)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Enables thinking, memory, emotions, and learning<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Coordinates balance and movement<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Responds to pain and danger (reflexes)<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udca1 Amazing Facts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>The brain has about 86 billion neurons \\u2013 as many stars as in the Milky Way galaxy!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Nerve signals travel at speeds up to 120 meters per second (268 mph)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The brain uses 20% of your body\'s oxygen and energy, but is only 2% of your weight<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your brain generates 12-25 watts of electricity \\u2013 enough to power a light bulb<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The brain has no pain receptors \\u2013 it cannot feel pain<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your spinal cord is about 45 cm (18 inches) long<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Organs<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/brain\\\" style=\\\"background: #44aa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83e\\udde0 Brain<\\/a>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Systems<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/muscular-system\\\" style=\\\"background: #44aa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83d\\udcaa Muscular System<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(2070,243,'footnotes',''),(2072,242,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2073,242,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2074,242,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2075,242,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:997ef14e505ddd4af49c620835e30da6'),(2087,245,'footnotes',''),(2088,245,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(2089,245,'_elementor_template_type','wp-page'),(2090,245,'_elementor_data',''),(2091,245,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2092,245,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2093,245,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2094,245,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:6235a6c47f65a3aca2fc5a7c56ad64e4'),(2095,246,'footnotes',''),(2096,246,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(2097,246,'_elementor_template_type','wp-page'),(2098,246,'_elementor_data',''),(2099,246,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2100,246,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2101,246,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2102,246,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:6235a6c47f65a3aca2fc5a7c56ad64e4'),(2103,242,'_wp_page_template','default'),(2104,242,'_elementor_page_settings','a:1:{s:10:\"hide_title\";s:3:\"yes\";}'),(2105,247,'footnotes',''),(2106,247,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(2107,247,'_elementor_template_type','wp-page'),(2108,247,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"0d9124b\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":{\"content_width\":\"full\",\"width\":{\"unit\":\"%\",\"size\":93.98},\"_flex_size\":\"none\",\"_element_width\":\"initial\"},\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"d070d25\",\"elType\":