>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 Functions<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Enables all body movements (walking, talking, smiling, jumping)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Maintains posture and body position<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Pumps blood (heart muscle works 24\\/7)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Moves food through digestive system<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Generates body heat (shivering warms you up)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Protects internal organs<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Controls breathing (diaphragm muscle)<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udca1 Amazing Facts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Your body has over 600 muscles, making up about 40% of your body weight<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The hardest working muscle is the heart \\u2013 it beats 100,000 times daily<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The largest muscle is the gluteus maximus (buttocks)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The smallest muscle is the stapedius in your ear (1mm long)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Muscles can only pull \\u2013 they cannot push<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>It takes 43 muscles to frown, but only 17 to smile!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your eye muscles move more than 100,000 times per day<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Organs<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/heart\\\" style=\\\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\u2764\\ufe0f Heart<\\/a>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related System<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/skeletal-system\\\" style=\\\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83e\\uddb4 Skeletal System<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(