eus maximus (buttocks)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The smallest muscle is the stapedius in your ear (1mm long)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Muscles can only pull \\u2013 they cannot push<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>It takes 43 muscles to frown, but only 17 to smile!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your eye muscles move more than 100,000 times per day<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Organs<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/heart\\\" style=\\\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\u2764\\ufe0f Heart<\\/a>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related System<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/skeletal-system\\\" style=\\\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83e\\uddb4 Skeletal System<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(2163,253,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2164,253,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2165,253,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2166,253,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:6235a6c47f65a3aca2fc5a7c56ad64e4'),(2167,253,'_wp_page_template','default'),(2168,253,'_elementor_page_settings','a:1:{s:10:\"hide_title\";s:3:\"yes\";}'),(2170,254,'_edit_lock','1781558627:1'),(2172,254,'_eb_attr',''),(2173,254,'footnotes',''),(2174,254,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(2175,254,'_elementor_template_type','wp-page'),(2176,254,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"fb97117\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"2724cb2\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"html\":\"<div style=\\\"max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; background: #fff0e8;\\\">\\r\\n    <h1 style=\\\"color: #ffaa44;\\\">\\ud83c\\udf7d\\ufe0f Digestive System<\\/h1>\\r\\n    \\r\\n    <div style=\\\"background: #000; border-radius: 15px; margin: 20px 0; overflow: hidden;\\\">\\r\\n        <iframe src=\\\"https:\\/\\/sketchfab.com\\/models\\/0031f9c064d44c42a251543dc500f525\\/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\\\"\\r\\n            style=\\\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\\\" \\r\\n            allow=\\\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\\\" \\r\\n            allowfullscreen>\\r\\n        <\\/iframe>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n\\r\\n    <div style=\\\"background: white; padding: 20px; border-radius: 15px;\\\">\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 What is the Digestive System?<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <p>The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that your body can absorb and use for energy, growth, and cell repair. It is a long, twisting tube that starts at the mouth and ends at the anus.<\\/p>\\r\\n        \\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd2c Main Parts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Mouth:<\\/strong> Chewing and saliva begin breaking down food<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Esophagus:<\\/strong> Tube that carries food to the stomach<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Stomach:<\\/strong> Churns food and mixes with strong acid<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Liver:<\\/strong> Produces bile to digest fats; filters toxins<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Gallbladder:<\\/strong> Stores bile from the liver<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Pancreas:<\\/strong> Produces enzymes to break down food<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Small Intestine:<\\/strong> Absorbs nutrients into blood (22 feet long)<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Large Intestine (Colon):<\\/strong> Absorbs water and forms waste<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li><strong>Rectum & Anus:<\\/strong> Stores and eliminates solid waste<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udcd6 Functions<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Breaks down food into tiny nutrients<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Absorbs vitamins, minerals, proteins, carbohydrates, and fats<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Produces energy from food<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Eliminates waste products from the body<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Houses beneficial bacteria that help digestion<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Protects against harmful bacteria in food<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udca1 Amazing Facts<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <ul>\\r\\n            <li>Your digestive system is about 30 feet (9 meters) long \\u2013 as tall as a school bus!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The small intestine is 22 feet long but only 1 inch wide<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your stomach produces new lining every 3-5 days to protect itself from acid<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Stomach acid is strong enough to dissolve a razor blade<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Your gut contains 100 trillion bacteria \\u2013 more than the cells in your body!<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>Food takes about 24-72 hours to travel through your digestive system<\\/li>\\r\\n            <li>The liver performs over 500 different functions<\\/li>\\r\\n        <\\/ul>\\r\\n\\r\\n        <h2>\\ud83d\\udd17 Related Organs<\\/h2>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/liver\\\" style=\\\"background: #ffaa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83d\\udd34 Liver<\\/a>\\r\\n        <a href=\\\"\\/biology\\/stomach\\\" style=\\\"background: #ffaa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\\\">\\ud83e\\udd58 Stomach<\\/a>\\r\\n    <\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"html\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(2178,255,'footnotes',''),(2180,254,'_elementor_version','4.1.3'),(2181,254,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed','1'),(2182,254,'_elementor_global_class_usage_indexed_preview','1'),(2183,254,'_elementor_migrations_state_d2a1','4.1.3:997ef14e505ddd4af49c620835e30da6'),(2184,256,'footnotes',''),(2185