ground: #44aaff; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">≡ƒ½ü Respiratory System</a>','Lungs','','inherit','closed','closed','','198-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:34:39','2026-06-15 20:34:39','',198,'http://localhost/biology/?p=206',0,'revision','',0),(207,1,'2026-06-15 20:35:48','2026-06-15 20:35:48','<h1 style=\"color: #cc6633;\">≡ƒö┤ Human Liver</h1>\n    <p><strong>Scientific Name:</strong> Jecur</p>\n    <p><strong>Location:</strong> Upper right side of the abdomen, below the diaphragm</p>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/a20686a3e4a54792bfede17ad32f4b1a/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Filters and detoxifies blood (removes toxins, alcohol, drugs)</li>\n            <li>Produces bile ΓÇô helps digest fats</li>\n            <li>Stores vitamins and minerals (A, D, E, K, B12, iron)</li>\n            <li>Produces proteins needed for blood clotting</li>\n            <li>Regulates blood sugar levels</li>\n            <li>Makes cholesterol and breaks down old red blood cells</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Right Lobe:</strong> Largest section</li>\n            <li><strong>Left Lobe:</strong> Smaller section</li>\n            <li><strong>Gallbladder:</strong> Stores bile (attached to liver)</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Largest internal organ ΓÇô weighs about 1.5 kg (3.3 pounds)</li>\n            <li>Performs over 500 vital functions</li>\n            <li>Only organ that can regenerate ΓÇô you can remove up to 75% and it grows back!</li>\n            <li>Filters about 1.4 liters of blood every minute</li>\n            <li>Produces 800-1000 ml of bile daily</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/digestive-system\" style=\"background: #cc6633; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">≡ƒì╜∩╕Å Digestive System</a>','Liver','','publish','closed','closed','','liver','','','2026-06-15 20:37:59','2026-06-15 20:37:59','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?page_id=207',0,'page','',0),(209,1,'2026-06-15 20:35:48','2026-06-15 20:35:48','','Liver','','inherit','closed','closed','','207-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:35:48','2026-06-15 20:35:48','',207,'http://localhost/biology/?p=209',0,'revision','',0),(211,1,'2026-06-15 20:37:55','2026-06-15 20:37:55','','Liver','','inherit','closed','closed','','207-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:37:55','2026-06-15 20:37:55','',207,'http://localhost/biology/?p=211',0,'revision','',0),(212,1,'2026-06-15 20:37:57','2026-06-15 20:37:57','','Liver','','inherit','closed','closed','','207-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:37:57','2026-06-15 20:37:57','',207,'http://localhost/biology/?p=212',0,'revision','',0),(213,1,'2026-06-15 20:37:59','2026-06-15 20:37:59','<h1 style=\"color: #cc6633;\">≡ƒö┤ Human Liver</h1>\n    <p><strong>Scientific Name:</strong> Jecur</p>\n    <p><strong>Location:</strong> Upper right side of the abdomen, below the diaphragm</p>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/a20686a3e4a54792bfede17ad32f4b1a/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Filters and detoxifies blood (removes toxins, alcohol, drugs)</li>\n            <li>Produces bile ΓÇô helps digest fats</li>\n            <li>Stores vitamins and minerals (A, D, E, K, B12, iron)</li>\n            <li>Produces proteins needed for blood clotting</li>\n            <li>Regulates blood sugar levels</li>\n            <li>Makes cholesterol and breaks down old red blood cells</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Right Lobe:</strong> Largest section</li>\n            <li><strong>Left Lobe:</strong> Smaller section</li>\n            <li><strong>Gallbladder:</strong> Stores bile (attached to liver)</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Largest internal organ ΓÇô weighs about 1.5 kg (3.3 pounds)</li>\n            <li>Performs over 500 vital functions</li>\n            <li>Only organ that can regenerate ΓÇô you can remove up to 75% and it grows back!</li>\n            <li>Filters about 1.4 liters of blood every minute</li>\n            <li>Produces 800-1000 ml of bile daily</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/digestive-system\" style=\"background: #cc6633; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">≡ƒì╜∩╕Å Digestive System</a>','Liver','','inherit','closed','closed','','207-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:37:59','2026-06-15 20:37:59','',207,'http://localhost/biology/?p=213',0,'revision','',0),(214,1,'2026-06-15 20:39:14','2026-06-15 20:39:14','<h1 style=\"color: #8866cc;\">≡ƒ½ÿ Human Kidneys</h1>\n    <p><strong>Scientific Name:</strong> Renes</p>\n    <p><strong>Location:</strong> Back of the abdomen, one on each side of the spine</p>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/06be91d207ef4b2ba327a9e1804a1aa5/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Filter waste and excess water from blood to make urine</li>\n            <li>Regulate blood pressure</li>\n            <li>Balance electrolytes (sodium, potassium, calcium)</li>\n            <li>Produce hormones ΓÇô erythropoietin (makes red blood cells)</li>\n            <li>Activate vitamin D for strong bones</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Renal Cortex:</strong> Outer layer</li>\n            <li><strong>Renal Medulla:</strong> Inner layer</li>\n            <li><strong>Nephrons:</strong> ~1 million tiny filtering units in each kidney</li>\n            <li><strong>Ureter:</strong> Tube that carries urine to the bladder</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Your kidneys filter all the blood in your body every 30 minutes</li>\n            <li>They filter about 200 liters of blood daily</li>\n            <li>Each kidney contains about 1 million nephrons</li>\n            <li>You can live a normal, healthy life with only one kidney</li>\n            <li>Kidneys produce about 1-2 liters of urine per day</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/circulatory-system\" style=\"background: #8866cc; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">Γ¥ñ∩╕Å Circulatory System</a>','Kidneys','','publish','closed','closed','','kidneys','','','2026-06-15 20:40:19','2026-06-15 20:40:19','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?page_id=214',0,'page','',0),(216,1,'2026-06-15 20:39:14','2026-06-15 20:39:14','','Kidneys','','inherit','closed','closed','','214-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:39:14','2026-06-15 20:39:14','',214,'http://localhost/biology/?p=216',0,'revision','',0),(217,1,'2026-06-15 20:40:15','2026-06-15 20:40:15','','Kidneys','','inherit','closed','closed','','214-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:40:15','2026-06-15 20:40:15','',214,'http://localhost/biology/?p=217',0,'revision','',0),(218,1,'2026-06-15 20:40:17','2026-06-15 20:40:17','','Kidneys','','inherit','closed','clos