ize of a football!</li>\n            <li>Food stays in your stomach for about 3-5 hours</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/digestive-system\" style=\"background: #cc8844; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">≡ƒì╜∩╕Å Digestive System</a>','Stomach','','publish','closed','closed','','stomach','','','2026-06-15 20:43:36','2026-06-15 20:43:36','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?page_id=220',0,'page','',0),(222,1,'2026-06-15 20:42:36','2026-06-15 20:42:36','','Stomach','','inherit','closed','closed','','220-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:42:36','2026-06-15 20:42:36','',220,'http://localhost/biology/?p=222',0,'revision','',0),(223,1,'2026-06-15 20:43:33','2026-06-15 20:43:33','','Stomach','','inherit','closed','closed','','220-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:43:33','2026-06-15 20:43:33','',220,'http://localhost/biology/?p=223',0,'revision','',0),(224,1,'2026-06-15 20:43:35','2026-06-15 20:43:35','','Stomach','','inherit','closed','closed','','220-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:43:35','2026-06-15 20:43:35','',220,'http://localhost/biology/?p=224',0,'revision','',0),(225,1,'2026-06-15 20:43:36','2026-06-15 20:43:36','<h1 style=\"color: #cc8844;\">≡ƒÑÿ Human Stomach</h1>\n    <p><strong>Scientific Name:</strong> Gaster</p>\n    <p><strong>Location:</strong> Upper left side of the abdomen</p>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/0031f9c064d44c42a251543dc500f525/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Stores and breaks down food using strong acids and enzymes</li>\n            <li>Mixes food with gastric juices to create \"chyme\" (semi-liquid food)</li>\n            <li>Kills harmful bacteria in food</li>\n            <li>Slowly releases food into the small intestine</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Cardia:</strong> Upper section ΓÇô where food enters</li>\n            <li><strong>Fundus:</strong> Upper curved section ΓÇô stores undigested food</li>\n            <li><strong>Body:</strong> Main central section ΓÇô mixes and breaks down food</li>\n            <li><strong>Pylorus:</strong> Bottom section ΓÇô connects to small intestine</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Produces about 2-3 liters of gastric acid daily</li>\n            <li>Stomach acid has a pH of 1.5-3.5 ΓÇô strong enough to dissolve metal!</li>\n            <li>The stomach\'s inner lining is replaced every 3-5 days</li>\n            <li>Can stretch from 75ml (empty) to 1 liter (full) ΓÇô size of a football!</li>\n            <li>Food stays in your stomach for about 3-5 hours</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/digestive-system\" style=\"background: #cc8844; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;\">≡ƒì╜∩╕Å Digestive System</a>','Stomach','','inherit','closed','closed','','220-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 20:43:36','2026-06-15 20:43:36','',220,'http://localhost/biology/?p=225',0,'revision','',0),(226,1,'2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 20:55:26','','Home','','publish','closed','closed','','home','','','2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 21:25:03','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?p=226',1,'nav_menu_item','',0),(227,1,'2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 20:55:27',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','227','','','2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 21:25:03','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?p=227',2,'nav_menu_item','',0),(228,1,'2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 20:55:27',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','','228','','','2026-06-15 21:25:03','2026-06-15 21:25:03','',0,'http://localhost