es thinking, memory, emotions, and learning</li>\n            <li>Coordinates balance and movement</li>\n            <li>Responds to pain and danger (reflexes)</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>The brain has about 86 billion neurons ΓÇô as many stars as in the Milky Way galaxy!</li>\n            <li>Nerve signals travel at speeds up to 120 meters per second (268 mph)</li>\n            <li>The brain uses 20% of your body\'s oxygen and energy, but is only 2% of your weight</li>\n            <li>Your brain generates 12-25 watts of electricity ΓÇô enough to power a light bulb</li>\n            <li>The brain has no pain receptors ΓÇô it cannot feel pain</li>\n            <li>Your spinal cord is about 45 cm (18 inches) long</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related Organs</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/brain\" style=\"background: #44aa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒºá Brain</a>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related Systems</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/muscular-system\" style=\"background: #44aa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒÆ¬ Muscular System</a>','Nervous System','','inherit','closed','closed','','242-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:15:05','2026-06-15 21:15:05','',242,'http://localhost/biology/?p=247',0,'revision','',0),(248,1,'2026-06-15 21:16:09','2026-06-15 21:16:09','<h1 style=\"color: #ff88aa;\"> Muscular System</h1>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/fb6fe7342b024ce6813cb724b71572be/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû What is the Muscular System?</h2>\n        <p>The muscular system is made of over 600 muscles that work together to move your body, maintain posture, pump blood, and generate heat. Every movement you make ΓÇô from blinking to running ΓÇô comes from muscles.</p>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Skeletal Muscles:</strong> Attached to bones ΓÇô control voluntary movement (600+ muscles)</li>\n            <li><strong>Smooth Muscles:</strong> Found in organs (stomach, intestines, blood vessels) ΓÇô work automatically</li>\n            <li><strong>Cardiac Muscle:</strong> Only in the heart ΓÇô never gets tired, beats automatically</li>\n            <li><strong>Tendons:</strong> Connect muscles to bones</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Enables all body movements (walking, talking, smiling, jumping)</li>\n            <li>Maintains posture and body position</li>\n            <li>Pumps blood (heart muscle works 24/7)</li>\n            <li>Moves food through digestive system</li>\n            <li>Generates body heat (shivering warms you up)</li>\n            <li>Protects internal organs</li>\n            <li>Controls breathing (diaphragm muscle)</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Your body has over 600 muscles, making up about 40% of your body weight</li>\n            <li>The hardest working muscle is the heart ΓÇô it beats 100,000 times daily</li>\n            <li>The largest muscle is the gluteus maximus (buttocks)</li>\n            <li>The smallest muscle is the stapedius in your ear (1mm long)</li>\n            <li>Muscles can only pull ΓÇô they cannot push</li>\n            <li>It takes 43 muscles to frown, but only 17 to smile!</li>\n            <li>Your eye muscles move more than 100,000 times per day</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related Organs</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/heart\" style=\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">Γ¥ñ∩╕Å Heart</a>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/skeletal-system\" style=\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒª┤ Skeletal System</a>','Muscular System','','publish','closed','closed','','muscular-system','','','2026-06-15 21:19:38','2026-06-15 21:19:38','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?page_id=248',0,'page','',0),(249,1,'2026-06-15 21:16:09','2026-06-15 21:16:09','','Muscular System','','inherit','closed','closed','','248-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:16:09','2026-06-15 21:16:09','',248,'http://localhost/biology/?p=249',0,'revision','',0),(251,1,'2026-06-15 21:19:35','2026-06-15 21:19:35','','Muscular System','','inherit','closed','closed','','248-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:19:35','2026-06-15 21:19:35','',248,'http://localhost/biology/?p=251',0,'revision','',0),(252,1,'2026-06-15 21:19:36','2026-06-15 21:19:36','','Muscular System','','inherit','closed','closed','','248-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:19:36','2026-06-15 21:19:36','',248,'http://localhost/biology/?p=252',0,'revision','',0),(253,1,'2026-06-15 21:19:38','2026-06-15 21:19:38','<h1 style=\"color: #ff88aa;\"> Muscular System</h1>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/fb6fe7342b024ce6813cb724b71572be/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû What is the Muscular System?</h2>\n        <p>The muscular system is made of over 600 muscles that work together to move your body, maintain posture, pump blood, and generate heat. Every movement you make ΓÇô from blinking to running ΓÇô comes from muscles.</p>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Skeletal Muscles:</strong> Attached to bones ΓÇô control voluntary movement (600+ muscles)</li>\n            <li><strong>Smooth Muscles:</strong> Found in organs (stomach, intestines, blood vessels) ΓÇô work automatically</li>\n            <li><strong>Cardiac Muscle:</strong> Only in the heart ΓÇô never gets tired, beats automatically</li>\n            <li><strong>Tendons:</strong> Connect muscles to bones</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Enables all body movements (walking, talking, smiling, jumping)</li>\n            <li>Maintains posture and body position</li>\n            <li>Pumps blood (heart muscle works 24/7)</li>\n            <li>Moves food through digestive system</li>\n            <li>Generates body heat (shivering warms you up)</li>\n            <li>Protects internal organs</li>\n            <li>Controls breathing (diaphragm muscle)</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Your body has over 600 muscles, making up about 40% of your body weight</li>\n            <li>The hardest working muscle is the heart ΓÇô it beats 100,000 times daily</li>\n            <li>The largest muscle is the gluteus maximus (buttocks)</li>\n            <li>The smallest muscle is the stapedius in your ear (1mm long)</li>\n            <li>Muscles can only pull ΓÇô they cannot push</li>\n            <li>It takes 43 muscles to frown, but only 17 to smile!</li>\n            <li>Your eye muscles move more than 100,000 times per day</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related Organs</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/heart\" style=\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">Γ¥ñ∩╕Å Heart</a>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related System</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/skeletal-system\" style=\"background: #ff88aa; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒª┤ Skeletal System</a>','Muscular System','','inherit','closed','closed','','248-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:19:38','2026-06-15 21:19:38','',248,'http://localhost/biology/?p=253',0,'revision','',0),(254,1,'2026-06-15 21:20:24','2026-06-15 21:20:24','<h1 style=\"color: #ffaa44;\">≡ƒì╜∩╕Å Digestive System</h1>\n        <iframe src=\"https://sketchfab.com/models/0031f9c064d44c42a251543dc500f525/embed?autospin=1&autostart=1&preload=1\"\n            style=\"width:100%; height:500px; border:none;\" \n            allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; xr-spatial-tracking\" \n            allowfullscreen>\n        </iframe>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû What is the Digestive System?</h2>\n        <p>The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that your body can absorb and use for energy, growth, and cell repair. It is a long, twisting tube that starts at the mouth and ends at the anus.</p>\n        <h2>≡ƒö¼ Main Parts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li><strong>Mouth:</strong> Chewing and saliva begin breaking down food</li>\n            <li><strong>Esophagus:</strong> Tube that carries food to the stomach</li>\n            <li><strong>Stomach:</strong> Churns food and mixes with strong acid</li>\n            <li><strong>Liver:</strong> Produces bile to digest fats; filters toxins</li>\n            <li><strong>Gallbladder:</strong> Stores bile from the liver</li>\n            <li><strong>Pancreas:</strong> Produces enzymes to break down food</li>\n            <li><strong>Small Intestine:</strong> Absorbs nutrients into blood (22 feet long)</li>\n            <li><strong>Large Intestine (Colon):</strong> Absorbs water and forms waste</li>\n            <li><strong>Rectum & Anus:</strong> Stores and eliminates solid waste</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒôû Functions</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Breaks down food into tiny nutrients</li>\n            <li>Absorbs vitamins, minerals, proteins, carbohydrates, and fats</li>\n            <li>Produces energy from food</li>\n            <li>Eliminates waste products from the body</li>\n            <li>Houses beneficial bacteria that help digestion</li>\n            <li>Protects against harmful bacteria in food</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒÆí Amazing Facts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Your digestive system is about 30 feet (9 meters) long ΓÇô as tall as a school bus!</li>\n            <li>The small intestine is 22 feet long but only 1 inch wide</li>\n            <li>Your stomach produces new lining every 3-5 days to protect itself from acid</li>\n            <li>Stomach acid is strong enough to dissolve a razor blade</li>\n            <li>Your gut contains 100 trillion bacteria ΓÇô more than the cells in your body!</li>\n            <li>Food takes about 24-72 hours to travel through your digestive system</li>\n            <li>The liver performs over 500 different functions</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h2>≡ƒöù Related Organs</h2>\n        <a href=\"/biology/liver\" style=\"background: #ffaa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒö┤ Liver</a>\n        <a href=\"/biology/stomach\" style=\"background: #ffaa44; color: white; padding: 8px 20px; border-radius: 20px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 5px;\">≡ƒÑÿ Stomach</a>','Digestive System','','publish','closed','closed','','digestive-system','','','2026-06-15 21:23:02','2026-06-15 21:23:02','',0,'http://localhost/biology/?page_id=254',0,'page','',0),(255,1,'2026-06-15 21:20:24','2026-06-15 21:20:24','','Digestive System','','inherit','closed','closed','','254-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:20:24','2026-06-15 21:20:24','',254,'http://localhost/biology/?p=255',0,'revision','',0),(256,1,'2026-06-15 21:22:59','2026-06-15 21:22:59','','Digestive System','','inherit','closed','closed','','254-revision-v1','','','2026-06-15 21:22:59','2026-06-15 21:22:59','',254,'http://localhost/biology/?p=256',0,'revision','',0),(257,1,'2026-06-15 21:23:00','2026-06-15 21:23:00','','Digestive System','','inherit','cl